            <ArticleTitle>Left main occlusion - a classic electrocardiogram.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>521-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/s00508-016-1007-8</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Left main occlusion is associated with a dire prognosis, as the left main supplies blood to &gt;75 % of the left ventricle. This is a case showing a classic electrocardiogram (ECG) together with the echocardiogram videos and images from coronary angiography.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
